<title>UK: Mexico's Posadas plans $50 million Eurobond.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Posadas plans $50 million Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican company Grupo Posadas is due to launch a $50 million five-year Eurobond next week, an official at lead manager ING Barings said on Friday.</p>
<p>There was no official price talk, the official said, but traders elsewhere expected a yield in the low- to mid-400s basis points over U.S. Treasury notes.</p>
<p>Grupo Posadas is Mexico's leading hotel operator and runs hotels throughout Latin America.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
